within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N05A_Antipsychotics.N05AH02_Clozapine;
model Clozapine_Parker2001_PD_theta_amplitude
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Parker_2001 :: theta amplitude (Increase in amplitude in the theta EEG frequency band)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 80,      // [µV s−1]
    Emax = 18,  // [µV s−1]
    EC50 = 0.00126,  // [kg/m3; ng ml−1 × 1e-06]
    gamma = 5.9,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng ml−1 per second
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 13000, Interval = 26),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Clozapine_Parker2001_PD_theta_amplitude</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Parker TJ et al., <i>British journal of pharmacology 132(1):151–158</i> 2001 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/sj.bjp.0703791\">doi:10.1038/sj.bjp.0703791</a>) — Increase in amplitude in the theta EEG frequency band [µV s−1] against clozapine ng ml−1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =         80 µV s−1   drug-free response (baseline) (E0, Q324)
  Emax  =         18 µV s−1   maximal effect term (Emax, Q320)
  EC50  =       1260 ng ml−1  exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma =        5.9          Hill coefficient (N, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng ml−1 of clozapine per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 80   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (1260 ng ml−1)  response 89
  exposure -> infinity  response 98</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Parker_2001: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Clozapine_Parker2001_PD_theta_amplitude;
